        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(feishu): keep log-value text truncation UTF-16 safe",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where Feishu debug logs containing emoji or supplementary-plane Unicode characters (e.g. 🚨, 😀, 🎉) could produce garbled text with lone surrogates when a log message exceeds 500 code units and the truncation boundary falls in the middle of a UTF-16 surrogate pair.\n\nThis affects two log-value truncation helpers in the feishu extension:\n\n- `sanitizeLogValue` (`card-action.ts`) — truncates chat-type resolution error messages at 500 code units\n- `formatFeishuWsErrorForLog` (`monitor.transport.ts`) — truncates WebSocket error messages at `FEISHU_WS_LOG_ERROR_MAX_LENGTH` (500 code units)\n\nThese two helpers were missed in the earlier sweep (c16bb8725a) that already covered `bot.ts` and `monitor.comment.ts` in the same extension — both using the identical `truncateUtf16Safe` import from `openclaw/plugin-sdk/text-utility-runtime`.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nReplace raw `.slice(0, N)` with the existing `truncateUtf16Safe` helper. `.slice()` operates on UTF-16 code units and can split a surrogate pair (e.g. 🚨 = `🚨`) in half, producing a lone high surrogate (`\\uD83D`) that renders as �. `truncateUtf16Safe` rounds down to the nearest safe code-point boundary.\n\nThis is the same mechanical fix that was already applied to `bot.ts` (lines 1007, 1074) and `monitor.comment.ts` in the feishu extension by the prior sweep c16bb8725a. No new dependencies or behavioral changes — the import path is identical.\n\nRisk note: log-only helpers, no user-visible message delivery surface affected. Operator-facing debug logs will see clean truncation instead of potential garbled characters.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNo direct end-user impact — these are operator-facing log helpers. Feishu operators reading debug logs will see correctly truncated error messages instead of potentially garbled characters when emoji appear at the 500-code-unit truncation boundary.\n\n## Evidence\n\n**Premise — `.slice(0, 500)` cuts surrogate pairs at the boundary used by both helpers:**\n\nConstructed a realistic log message with an emoji (🚨) positioned so its UTF-16 surrogate pair straddles the 500-code-unit boundary (first surrogate at index 499, second at index 500). `.slice(0, 500)` includes only the high surrogate, producing a lone surrogate. `truncateUtf16Safe` correctly rounds down to 499 code units.\n\n```\n$ node -e \"\nfunction hasLoneSurrogate(s) {\n  for (let i = 0; i < s.length; i++) {\n    const code = s.charCodeAt(i);\n    if (code >= 0xD800 && code <= 0xDBFF) {\n      if (i + 1 >= s.length || s.charCodeAt(i + 1) < 0xDC00 || s.charCodeAt(i + 1) > 0xDFFF) return true;\n      i++;\n    } else if (code >= 0xDC00 && code <= 0xDFFF) return true;\n  }\n  return false;\n}\n\nconst MAX = 500;\nconst msg = 'x'.repeat(499) + '🚨' + ' connection timeout';\n\nconsole.log('BEFORE .slice(0,' + MAX + '): len=' + msg.slice(0, MAX).length + ' lone=' + hasLoneSurrogate(msg.slice(0, MAX)));\n// Output: BEFORE .slice(0,500): len=500 lone=true ❌\n\"\n```\n\n**Negative control — old code produces garbled output, fix eliminates it:**\n\n```\n$ node --import tsx -e \"\nimport { truncateUtf16Safe } from './src/plugin-sdk/text-utility-runtime.ts';\n\nconst MAX = 500;\nconst msg = 'x'.repeat(499) + '🚨' + ' rest of error details';\nconst old = msg.slice(0, MAX);         // OLD PATTERN (missed by prior sweep)\nconst fix = truncateUtf16Safe(msg, MAX); // NEW PATTERN (this PR)\n\nfunction hasLone(str) { /* ... same as above ... */ }\n\nconsole.log('OLD .slice(0,500) tail:', JSON.stringify(old.slice(-6)));\n// → 'xxxxx\\\\ud83d'  ❌ LONE HIGH SURROGATE (garbled)\n\nconsole.log('NEW truncateUtf16Safe:', fix.length);\n// → 499  ✅ rounded down below surrogate pair\n\"\n```\n\n**Actual output demonstrating the fix in context:**\n\n| Method | Length | Lone Surrogate | Tail | Correct? |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `.slice(0, 500)` (old) | 500 | true ❌ | `\"xxxxx\\ud83d\"` | No — renders as � |\n| `truncateUtf16Safe(x, 500)` (new) | 499 | false ✅ | `\"xxxxxx\"` | Yes — clean truncation |\n\n**Changed files (diff):**\n\n- `extensions/feishu/src/card-action.ts` — `sanitizeLogValue`: `.slice(0, 500)` → `truncateUtf16Safe(x, 500)`, +1 import\n- `extensions/feishu/src/monitor.transport.ts` — `formatFeishuWsErrorForLog`: `.slice(0, N)` → `truncateUtf16Safe(x, N)`, +1 import\n\n**Test run:** `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs run extensions/feishu/` — passed (exit 0).\n\n**What was not tested:** Live Feishu WebSocket error logs with emoji content across the boundary. No live Feishu credentials available in this checkout. The code change is identical to the already-shipped fix in `bot.ts` (c16bb8725a), using the same import path and helper function.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
        "branch": "fix/feishu-utf16-truncate",
